\section*{Kobayashi Conjecture: Hyperbolic Compact Kähler Manifolds Have Ample Canonical Bundle}

\subsection{OpenAI's claim}
Every positive-dimensional compact Kähler manifold without nonconstant entire curves is claimed to be projective with ample canonical bundle. The cited manuscript argues for that result; its relation to this problem is specified below.

\subsection{Outline of the argument}
Manuscript 1 (family 051, 2026-09-23): Hyperbolicity bounds derivatives of holomorphic discs, and a Hardy-space frame realizes center-fixed variations with an area-Hessian identity. Disc envelopes give nef canonical weights, while the complementary variation estimate forces a volume lower bound; these positivity controls lead to canonical ampleness.

\subsection{Scope relative to this problem}
Manuscript 1 (family 051, 2026-09-23): The main theorem assumes compact connected Kähler geometry and absence of nonconstant entire curves and concludes canonical ampleness, including projectivity; this is precisely the catalogue compact hyperbolic formulation.

\subsection{Formal verification}
Family 051 has no Lean scope page in this snapshot; no formalization of these manuscript results is listed.

This site has not executed the Lean files or checked their dependencies. These descriptions report the scope of the linked declarations, rather than a new verification of the proofs.

\subsection{Status caveat}
OpenAI attributes these results to an internal model. Its release notice cautions that results lacking full formalization can contain mistakes. This site has not independently assessed the proofs; a solved label records the scope of the reported claim.

\subsection{Sources}
